### Step 2 – Manage permissions

#### What I did
- Opened a report → Share → Manage permissions.
- Viewed:
  - Direct access (users I shared with),
  - Links (shareable links),
  - Workspace access (roles: Viewer/Member/Contributor/Admin).
- Practiced removing and modifying permissions.
- Checked permissions of the dataset (semantic model) via:
  Workspace → … → Manage permissions.

#### What I learned
- A user can gain report access through:
  - direct share,
  - workspace role,
  - app access.
- You cannot remove a user that has access via the workspace (only from direct share).
- Dataset permissions are separate from report permissions.
- Permissions can be:
  - Can view
  - Can reshare (if enabled)
  - Workspace roles that give broader rights

